  "content_text": "\r\n    \r\n        \r\n    \r\n    \r\n        \n            Manhattan Active SCALE Documentation\r\n        WM Capture Inventory Attributes\r\n    \r\n    \r\n         \n                Collapse All\n                Expand All\n            \r\n        View with Navigation Tools\r\n    \r\n    \r\nIntegration Endpoints\r\n > Exit points\r\n > WM Capture Inventory Attributes\r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \r\n        The system provides an exit point WM Capture Inventory Attributes , that should be used to let the system know if it should prompt for inventory attributes.\r\n\r\nThe exit point should return 'YES' to capture attirbutes, any other return value will skip the attributes entry.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe following example represents a sample implementation of the WM Capture Inventory Attributes/em> exit point program using a stored procedure. \r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n        \r\n            \r\n                Sample exit point program for WM Capture Inventory Attributes exit point\r\n\r\n                \r\n                    \r\n                        Copy Code\r\n                    \r\n                \r\n            \r\n\r\n            \r\n                \r\n                    \r\nCREATE PROCEDURE [EXP_WmCaptureInventoryAttributes] (\r\n    @SESSIONVALUE xml,\r\n    @ITEM nvarchar(50),\r\n    @COMPANY nvarchar(25),\r\n    @LOCATION nvarchar(25),\r\n    @RETURNVALUE nvarchar(max) output\r\n)\r\nAS \r\n    SET NOCOUNT ON; \r\n    --insert custom sql \r\nSet @RETURNVALUE = 'YES'\r\n\r\n                \r\n            \r\n        \r\n    \r\n\r\n\r\n \n            \n            \r\n        \r\n    \r\n    \r\n        \n  ©2026 Manhattan Associates. All Rights Reserved.\n\r\n    \r\n    \r\n\r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \r\n",
  "search_text": "\r\n    \n\r\n        \r\n    \n\r\n    \n\r\n        \n            \nManhattan Active SCALE Documentation\n\r\n        \n\nWM Capture Inventory Attributes\n\n\r\n    \n\r\n    \n\r\n         \n                Collapse All\n                Expand All\n            \r\n        View with Navigation Tools\r\n    \n\r\n    \n\n\n\n\r\nIntegration Endpoints\r\n > Exit points\r\n > WM Capture Inventory Attributes\n\n\n\n\r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \n\r\n        \nThe system provides an exit point WM Capture Inventory Attributes , that should be used to let the system know if it should prompt for inventory attributes.\n\r\n\r\n\nThe exit point should return 'YES' to capture attirbutes, any other return value will skip the attributes entry.\n\r\n\r\n\n \n\r\n\r\n\nThe following example represents a sample implementation of the WM Capture Inventory Attributes/em> exit point program using a stored procedure. \n\r\n\r\n\n\r\n    \n\r\n        \n\r\n            \n\r\n                \nSample exit point program for WM Capture Inventory Attributes exit point\n\r\n\r\n                \n\r\n                    \n\r\n                        Copy Code\r\n                    \n\r\n                \n\r\n            \n\r\n\r\n            \n\r\n                \n\r\n                    \n\r\nCREATE PROCEDURE [EXP_WmCaptureInventoryAttributes] (\r\n    @SESSIONVALUE xml,\r\n    @ITEM nvarchar(50),\r\n    @COMPANY nvarchar(25),\r\n    @LOCATION nvarchar(25),\r\n    @RETURNVALUE nvarchar(max) output\r\n)\r\nAS \r\n    SET NOCOUNT ON; \r\n    --insert custom sql \r\nSet @RETURNVALUE = 'YES'\r\n\n\r\n                \n\r\n            \n\r\n        \n\r\n    \n\r\n\n\r\n\r\n\n \n\n            \n            \r\n        \r\n    \n\r\n    \n\r\n        \n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n©2026 Manhattan Associates. All Rights Reserved.\n\n\r\n    \n\r\n    \r\n\r\n    \r\n    \r\n    \r\n",
